 {"id":"fabro-dc81","title":"Postlude: re-resolve [run.pull_request] from the run branch tip or emit a takes-effect-next-run notice","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T18:50:37.532Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T19:00:18.678Z","description":"In lib/components/fabro-workflow/src/pipeline/publish.rs (run-spec/postlude settings resolution), either re-resolve [run.pull_request] from the run branch tip when the run's own diff edits its workflow.toml, or append a 'takes effect next run' notice to the PR body. Basis: run-spec snapshot at creation (event seq 1) carried auto_merge = true — the exact value this run's seed fabro-6a5a set to false — so PR #107's postlude executed under pre-fix settings and the two recurring failures the seed exists to kill persisted on the fixing run itself (postlude activity until 18:45:34, ~1m46s after completion). Expected effect: no misleading failure/warn on the run that ships a fix. Distinct mechanism from fabro-6a5a (config value vs engine resolution) and from fabro-9f97/fabro-1409. Basis: run 01M23Q0VM3YVECMSHDNX2HH3PJ, workflow version 3b17faf145735aa14caf619a38c0b079a1ff1c91acf24211c9ab08a2612c6f6f, commit 30653c1043a48ac2c1834c761492b5ac10ea11d9","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-d114","title":"Revert auto_merge=false from fabro-6a5a (PR #107): user decision — auto-merge must stay; 6a5a premise was stale","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T19:01:56.361Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T19:10:03.463Z","assignee":"agent","description":"USER DECISION (2026-09-09, chat): 'automerge muss bleiben' — option A of the A/B/C grill fork. PR #107 (fabro-6a5a) set auto_merge=false in .fabro/workflows/develop/workflow.toml on the premise that the enableAutoMerge GraphQL call 'deterministically fails' on this repo. Verification 2026-09-09 disproves the premise: repo setting allow_auto_merge=true, and PRs #102 and #107 itself carried ACTIVE auto-merge (enabled_by: denkhaus = engine PAT, merge_method squash) — GitHub merged today's run PRs (#96-#102) automatically. The failure evidence cited by fabro-6a5a dates from 2026-09-02 (run 01M0WWKAQCWZC0Q0JK019H0ZC7, worker log 16:44:33), before the repo setting era. The valid half of fabro-6a5a (resolve_pr_model fix + regression tests, ~53s postlude saving) is NOT affected and stays. Wanted: after #107 merges, revert ONLY the auto_merge hunk (false->true) plus its justification comment; new comment documents the user decision and the stale premise. Agent implements directly (explicit user assignment in chat). Acceptance: workflow.toml has auto_merge=true with the decision-documented comment; next run PR carries active auto-merge; no other #107 content reverted. Basis: grill session 2026-09-09, gh api checks on pulls/102 and pulls/107 (auto_merge objects), repo settings allow_auto_merge=true. CLOSED: revert commit b9f7c75e2 pushed to denkhaus (b9f7c75e2 range) — auto_merge=true restored with decision-documented comment; no other #107 content touched.","labels":["revision","workflows"],"closedAt":"2026-09-09T19:10:03.463Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-9d2f","title":"Engine: a steered/failed stage's abandoned worktree diff must not be committed by later cycles — quarantine residue between cycles","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T19:24:04.137Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T19:24:04.137Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"INCIDENT 2026-09-09 (run 01M23RQRCB748R4VRXA2WE6BZ0, PR #109): the duplicate-6a5a cycle was steered to fail at implementer (19:14:37Z); the implementer correctly 'abandoned in place, not committed' its diff (auto_merge=false in 3 workflow.tomls + pull_request.rs logging). The Blocked route returned to the planner, which claimed a DIFFERENT seed (fabro-e702); the next cycle ran on the SAME worktree and its deterministic closeout committed EVERYTHING — the abandoned residue rode into PR #109 alongside e702's legitimate prompt work and was approved by a reviewer who saw loop files as counts-only. Line-watch closed #109 unmerged (auto-merge would have landed the residue and re-contradicted the recorded user auto-merge decision fabro-d114). Wanted: when a stage fails (or is steered to abort), the engine quarantines/resets the uncommitted worktree state before the next cycle starts — or the closeout's diff assembly only includes files touched since the CURRENT seed's claim, with residue surfaced as a blocking anomaly. Also worth covering: one-seed-per-run discipline after a mid-run failure (the planner re-planned a second seed in the same run — the loop Bound expected by the planner prompt). Acceptance: engine test proving a failed stage's residue cannot reach a later cycle's commit/PR; closeout diff scoping test; clippy/fmt clean. Basis: run 01M23RQRCB748R4VRXA2WE6BZ0 journal + events (stage.failed 19:14:47Z, cycle-2 claim fabro-e702), PR #109 diff, line-watch close 2026-09-09 ~19:30Z.","labels":["engine","workflows"]}
-{"id":"fabro-c0e5","title":"Evidence capture must flag out-of-spec seed-work files (residue detection), not just demote loop files to counts-only","status":"in_progress","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T19:24:04.235Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T19:32:14.820Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"Same incident as the residue seed (run 01M23RQRCB748R4VRXA2WE6BZ0, PR #109): the evidence capture classified .fabro/workflows/*/workflow.toml changes as loop churn (counts-only), so the reviewer NEVER SAW that the PR's core semantic content (auto_merge=false across three workflows) was out-of-spec residue from a steered-failed cycle — and approved. The known classifier painpoint (promote loop files when the SPEC names them, journaled in run 01M230P8RGN) covers expected loop-work; this is the inverse case: loop/seed-work files changed that the spec does NOT name must surface as a named, diffed ANOMALY section, not disappear into counts. Wanted: the evidence capture (and/or the reviewer prompt) treats any changed file outside the claimed seed's spec scope as a first-class finding: full diff + 'not named by the seed spec' marker; the reviewer must adjudicate it explicitly (residue vs adjacent repair vs scope creep). Acceptance: evidence.nu/reviewer test with an out-of-spec workflow.toml change proving it appears named+diffed, not counts-only. Basis: PR #109 evidence + review (approved with invisible auto_merge flip), run 01M230P8RGN journal (the classifier painpoint), PR #109 close evidence.","labels":["engine","workflows"]}
